    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mywnjrmkb22z",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Artificial Analysis finally moves to closed benchmarks (goodbye & good riddance, GDPval-AA), and finds that open weights models are falling  further behind than they had previously measured. Take with a grain of salt, but matches the general vibes that we haven't seen a Fable-class open model.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mywnjrmkb22z",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T11:29:15.081Z",
      "likes": 159,
      "replies": 17,
      "reposts": 15,
      "score": 7.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myvqffe2d22q",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Google's Genie 4 world model: \"Scene: A Victorian high tea. Character: A mouse in appropriate garb.\"\n\n\"A porcupine walks by\"\n\n\"The mouse grows wings\"\n\n\"It flies\"\n\nThis is realtime & I can walk around freely.\n\nIt is glitchy, but also impossibly advanced compared to where we were a couple years ago.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myvqffe2d22q",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T02:47:49.493Z",
      "likes": 102,
      "replies": 4,
      "reposts": 10,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 25.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myvcgatpbs2q",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Important, but not unexpected, finding that experts working with AI agents are swayed by the positions of the AI, even if they think they aren't.\n\nIf your independent judgement matters on a task, you need to be deliberate about when in the process to bring in AI. www.anthropic.com/research/age...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myvcgatpbs2q",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-27T22:37:45.931Z",
      "likes": 84,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 17,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 29.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myxroqjxyc2f",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Yeah, no shit. A non-trivial number of HCI, HAI, and HRI studies since forever have more or less the same thing.\n\nBut I guess this study get press coverage because it is done by Anthropic",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myxroqjxyc2f",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T22:16:16.423Z",
      "likes": 20,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 6.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myxfev6zps2m",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I'm really sorry if you are well-meaning. I'm sure you are just as much a victim of the attention-sucking onslaught that is publicly available AI. I'm overwhelmed, and the signal is lost in the noise.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myxfev6zps2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-28T18:36:00.868Z",
      "likes": 6,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 9.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myxf3cbeqs2m",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "If I were to tally all the requests for 5, 10, 15, or 20 minute interviews from companies, high-school students, and people seeking graduate admissions, I think it would now be a full time job.\n\nI assume this is an effect of AI recommendations plus the ease with which one can shotgun emails with AI",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myxf3cbeqs2m",
